{"data":{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.23610719","type":"dois","attributes":{"doi":"10.5281/zenodo.23610719","prefix":"10.5281","suffix":"zenodo.23610719","identifiers":[{"identifier":"oai:zenodo.org:23610719","identifierType":"oai"}],"alternateIdentifiers":[{"alternateIdentifierType":"oai","alternateIdentifier":"oai:zenodo.org:23610719"}],"creators":[{"name":"Wang, Yuze","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Yuze","familyName":"Wang","affiliation":["Shenqiaohui Sports Science and Technology Innovation Center, Guangming District, Shenzhen, Guangdong, China"],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Wu, Zhongtang","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Zhongtang","familyName":"Wu","affiliation":["School of Physical Education, Shenzhen University, Shenzhen, Guangdong, China","University–Industry Joint Laboratory for Motion Perception, Shenzhen University, Shenzhen, Guangdong, China"],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Yang, Wenli","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Wenli","familyName":"Yang","affiliation":["Shenzhen Shenkun Technology Co., Ltd., Shenzhen, Guangdong, China"],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Zhou, Linjing","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Linjing","familyName":"Zhou","affiliation":["School of Psychology, Shenzhen University, Shenzhen, Guangdong, China"],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Ruan, Caixian","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Caixian","familyName":"Ruan","affiliation":["School of Physical Education, Shenzhen University, Shenzhen, Guangdong, China","University–Industry Joint Laboratory for Motion Perception, Shenzhen University, Shenzhen, Guangdong, China"],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Li, Wanna","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Wanna","familyName":"Li","affiliation":["Shenzhen University"],"nameIdentifiers":[]}],"titles":[{"title":"Processed fNIRS data and analysis code for low-altitude flight-scene viewing"}],"publisher":"Zenodo","container":{},"publicationYear":2026,"subjects":[{"subject":"functional near-infrared spectroscopy"},{"subject":"fNIRS"},{"subject":"low-altitude flight scenes"},{"subject":"passive viewing"},{"subject":"wide-field presentation"},{"subject":"digital grayscale"},{"subject":"optical flow"},{"subject":"regional hemodynamics"}],"contributors":[],"dates":[{"date":"2026-10-24","dateType":"Issued"}],"language":"en","types":{"ris":"DATA","bibtex":"misc","citeproc":"dataset","schemaOrg":"Dataset","resourceType":"","resourceTypeGeneral":"Dataset"},"relatedIdentifiers":[{"relationType":"IsVersionOf","relatedIdentifier":"10.5281/zenodo.23610718","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"}],"relatedItems":[],"sizes":[],"formats":[],"version":"v7","rightsList":[{"rights":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","rightsUri":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode","schemeUri":"https://spdx.org/licenses/","rightsIdentifier":"cc-by-4.0","rightsIdentifierScheme":"SPDX"},{"rights":"MIT License","rightsUri":"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT","schemeUri":"https://spdx.org/licenses/","rightsIdentifier":"mit","rightsIdentifierScheme":"SPDX"}],"descriptions":[{"description":"This record contains processed functional near-infrared spectroscopy (fNIRS) data and analysis resources for an exploratory study of passive viewing of low-altitude flight scenes. Twenty-three participants were included in the primary analyses of four 60-s passenger-perspective videos presented in a stationary cabin with wide-field projection.The archive Minimal_Dataset_v7.zip contains native-rate processed oxygenated- and deoxygenated-hemoglobin channel time series, experimental event records, video-feature time series, saved participant-specific design matrices, channel-selection and quality-control records, participant-level coefficients, group statistics, and analysis and plotting scripts. Documentation includes a README, a data dictionary, a file index, and software environment specifications.The resources support two primary questions: regional hemoglobin differences between video viewing and white-cross fixation (RQ1), and within-video associations of digital grayscale and mean optical-flow magnitude with regional hemodynamic time series (RQ2). The analysis workflow starts from processed fNIRS signals and saved design matrices. Original fNIRS recordings and stimulus video files are not included in this record.","descriptionType":"Abstract"},{"description":"The data and documentation in Minimal_Dataset_v7.zip are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International license (CC BY 4.0). This applies to the contents of data/ and docs/, README.md, FILE_INDEX.csv, and environment/requirements-lock.txt, to the extent that the rights holders are entitled to license those materials.The author-generated scripts code/_candidate_io.py, code/reproduce_main_models.py, and code/plot_saved_results.py are licensed under the MIT License. The corresponding copyright holder is Yuze Wang. The MIT copyright and permission notice is provided below.These licenses apply to the specified components separately; they are not alternative licenses for the entire archive. Third-party software dependencies remain subject to their respective licenses. This record does not include or license the original fNIRS recordings or stimulus video files.MIT LicenseCopyright (c) 2026 Yuze WangPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copyof this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to dealin the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rightsto use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sellcopies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software isfurnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in allcopies or substantial portions of the Software.THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS ORIMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THEAUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHERLIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THESOFTWARE.","descriptionType":"Other"}],"geoLocations":[],"fundingReferences":[],"xml":"","url":"https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23610719","contentUrl":null,"metadataVersion":0,"schemaVersion":"http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4","source":"api","isActive":true,"state":"findable","reason":null,"viewCount":0,"viewsOverTime":[],"downloadCount":0,"downloadsOverTime":[],"referenceCount":0,"citationCount":0,"citationsOverTime":[],"partCount":0,"partOfCount":0,"versionCount":0,"versionOfCount":1,"created":"2026-10-24T06:45:29.000Z","registered":"2026-10-24T06:45:29.000Z","published":"2026","updated":"2026-10-24T06:45:29.000Z"},"relationships":{"client":{"data":{"id":"cern.zenodo","type":"clients"}},"provider":{"data":{"id":"cern","type":"providers"}},"media":{"data":{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.23610719","type":"media"}},"references":{"data":[]},"citations":{"data":[]},"parts":{"data":[]},"partOf":{"data":[]},"versions":{"data":[]},"versionOf":{"data":[{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.23610718","type":"dois"}]}}}}